	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Refine, rewrite, and reshape text via the Claude CLI.

USAGE

  1. Keyword:  Type `rw` in Alfred. Templates appear immediately; type more to filter
     (e.g. `rw conc`). The rewritten clipboard text is auto-pasted into the active app.
  2. Universal Action:  Select text anywhere → invoke "Refine via Claude" → pick a template.

SETUP

  1. Install the Claude CLI: https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/claude-code
  2. Sign in:  claude /login
  3. From the repo root:  ./install.sh         (end users)
                     or:  ./install.sh --dev   (contributors — symlinks for live sync)

TEMPLATES

  Drop a new .md file into ~/.config/claude-refine/templates/ to add a refinement
  option. Each file = one Alfred option. See templates/README.md in the repo.

REPO

  https://github.com/mthines/alfred-claude-refine</string>
